The bundled English word list in `words-en.json` is derived from the word list
shipped with the `wordninja` Python package:

    https://pypi.org/project/wordninja/
    https://github.com/keredson/wordninja

`wordninja` is distributed under the MIT License. The list has been converted
from a newline separated text file to JSON and de-duplicated; the words and
their frequency order are unchanged.

The segmentation algorithm follows the approach described in:

    https://stackoverflow.com/questions/8870261/how-to-split-text-without-spaces-into-list-of-words

The camel case splitting logic was originally inspired by the
`split-camelcase-to-words` package:

    https://www.npmjs.com/package/split-camelcase-to-words
